{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02500",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.1,
      "end_seconds": 3.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Right then, come on in."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.95,
      "end_seconds": 7.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 8.87,
      "end_seconds": 12.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "good morning, doctor i came along to help out"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.12,
      "end_seconds": 21.43,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "Yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit. So what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 23.5,
      "end_seconds": 26.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "We came cos of cold feet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.04,
      "end_seconds": 31.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "what's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.76,
      "end_seconds": 35.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "About... well, about a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.3,
      "end_seconds": 39.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "how much trouble does it give you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.05,
      "end_seconds": 43.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "A eight out of ten, I suppose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.43,
      "end_seconds": 49.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 49.95,
      "end_seconds": 56.56,
      "duration_seconds": 6.61,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.44,
      "end_seconds": 59.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.83,
      "end_seconds": 75.17,
      "duration_seconds": 13.34,
      "text": "oh, and hair loss on my shins. That's been about the same, about a week. There's cramping in my calves when I walk as well"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 76.41,
      "end_seconds": 85.94,
      "duration_seconds": 9.53,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.82,
      "end_seconds": 92.97,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Mild, really. I notice it it more with walking."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.84,
      "end_seconds": 100.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.45,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something? Take your time, there's no rush"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.09,
      "end_seconds": 102.91,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "I've got high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.9,
      "end_seconds": 105.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "and besides that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.21,
      "end_seconds": 112.86,
      "duration_seconds": 6.65,
      "text": "I have diabetes, for about a year. I have gout. I've got low haemoglobin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.89,
      "end_seconds": 116.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Is that everything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.93,
      "end_seconds": 128.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.35,
      "text": "Okay, I can see high cholesterol and diabetes in your file as well. Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.82,
      "end_seconds": 137.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.15,
      "text": "I think I reacted to some antibiotic once, years ago. I don't remember which one, or what happened exactly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 148.14,
      "end_seconds": 150.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "Alright, do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 152.4,
      "end_seconds": 158.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.89,
      "end_seconds": 160.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.78,
      "end_seconds": 166.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 167.65,
      "end_seconds": 169.55,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.1,
      "end_seconds": 172.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.48,
      "end_seconds": 177.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.52,
      "end_seconds": 191.2,
      "duration_seconds": 12.68,
      "text": "Simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night. Sitagliptin, 100 milligrams, once a day for my sugar. Allopurinol. I take it 100 milligrams, maybe, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.79,
      "end_seconds": 196.93,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.64,
      "end_seconds": 206.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.64,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I take iron tablets, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.87,
      "end_seconds": 222.12,
      "duration_seconds": 5.25,
      "text": "Any pain at rest, back pain, chest pain or fever at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.52,
      "end_seconds": 239.44,
      "duration_seconds": 15.92,
      "text": "No, no pain at rest, no back pain, no chest pain. I did have a slow-healing toe sore at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.83,
      "end_seconds": 242.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "is your mobility otherwise okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 243.7,
      "end_seconds": 245.26,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "no, nothing there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 246.26,
      "end_seconds": 256.81,
      "duration_seconds": 10.55,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 36.8 degrees, heart rate 73, SpO2 97 percent on room air, BP is 113 over 73."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.93,
      "end_seconds": 269.65,
      "duration_seconds": 11.72,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Going by what you've described, it fits best with peripheral arterial disease. It could also be a nerve problem, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.5,
      "end_seconds": 275.29,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.2,
      "end_seconds": 292.43,
      "duration_seconds": 16.23,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's peripheral arterial disease, and we'll know more once the an ultrasound of the leg arteries is back. I'd like to arrange an ultrasound of the leg arteries for claudication."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 294.22,
      "end_seconds": 298.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.08,
      "text": "okay, so do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.99,
      "end_seconds": 327.24,
      "duration_seconds": 28.25,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a cholesterol test for arterial disease. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. We'll begin with clopidogrel, 75 milligrams, once a day, long term. That's for arterial disease. Stop smoking and walk until the pain starts, then rest, and repeat daily. I'll also refer you to the vascular clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 329.08,
      "end_seconds": 344.33,
      "duration_seconds": 15.25,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. See me again in four weeks. Is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.03,
      "end_seconds": 349.94,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.53,
      "end_seconds": 352.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "So, have a good day."
    }
  ]
}